    "table": {
      "continued": false,
      "footnotes": [
        "[After Building trade:] Working hours, nine per day. Time and a half paid for overtime. Free temporary sleeping quarters provided on the building site and communal messing at cheap rates.",
        "[After Shipbuilding and engineering:] Overtime, time and a half. Night work, double time.",
        "[After Transport workers:] Chinese Bus Co.: working hours, nine per day. Free uniform. Bonus at end of year, three days' pay. European Bus Co.: nine hours a day. Free uniform. One month's salary bonus.",
        "[After Female workers in factories:] Working hours from 7 a.m. to 5 p.m. One hour off at midday. Overtime from 6 p.m. to 9 p.m. at day rates.",
        "[After Domestic servants:] With free lodging, and, with Chinese employers, generally free board.",
        "Note.—The rates of pay of Government employees are much the same as those of a similar category in private employ."
      ],
